# Keep the build context small and — more importantly — keep secrets OUT of
# the image. Anything not excluded here is baked into an image layer by
# `COPY . .`, and image layers are readable by anyone who can pull the image
# or run `docker history`. Deleting a secret in a later layer does not remove
# it from the earlier one.
#
# encryption.key and service-account-key.json were previously NOT excluded,
# so every build embedded the live Firebase service-account credentials and
# the key that decrypts every stored device credential. They are now
# excluded here and supplied at RUNTIME as read-only bind mounts instead —
# see docker-compose.yml.

# --- Secrets: never in an image layer ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
encryption.key
service-account-key.json
static/js/firebase-config.js

# --- Local state that must come from the host volume, not the image ---
instance/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Python build artefacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# --- Virtualenvs ---
env/
venv/
.venv/
venv-ci/
include/
lib/
lib64/
bin/
share/
pyvenv.cfg

# --- Tooling / CI / docs: not needed at runtime ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.gemini/
tests/
migration/
*.md
*.log
*.pid

# --- Compose files are read by the daemon, not needed inside the image ---
docker-compose*.yml
